H.E.R.O. (1984) was designed by John Van Ryzin and published by Activision;
the Commodore 64 version was adapted by The Softworks. The game, its
program, artwork, sounds and data, and the H.E.R.O. and ACTIVISION
trademarks belong to their current rights holders.

The game logic in src/hero_*.c is a translation of the original program
for interoperability; it reads all of the game's data (graphics, levels,
sound tables) from the player's own tape image at run time. This project
contains and distributes no tape images and no data, graphics or sounds
taken from them, and no Commodore ROMs (the one text row drawn with the C64
character ROM uses an original lookalike font).

This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Activision, The
Softworks, Commodore or any successor.
